WEBVTT

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.380
You're at least 300 years older than the ones in the last chamber.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.100
You sure you can't read any of this?

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.240
Nope.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.000
How about you?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.380
Well, I think this says tall guys are popular.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.640
Mmm, you're a budding linguist.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.580
- Let's get a shot of that one.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.090
I wonder what happened to them.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.910
- It is kind of weird.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:48.910
Not a single biosign on the entire planet.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.850
Tucker, you about finished down there, Tripp?

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.830
- You can't believe these ruins, sir.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.060
We've been through two dozen chambers.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.150
No telling how many more there are.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.860
- I'm afraid you're not gonna find out today.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.900
That storm we told you about hasn't changed course.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.560
Most of you are going to need to get back to Enterprise.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.640
We'll just finish up with Mr. Tall and Popular.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.790
We should be back to the shuttle pod in five, six minutes.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.220
Don't take any longer than that.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.250
Archer out.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.010
Captain, we have another storm.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.140
Another one?

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:26.610
The discharges are more intense.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.630
It's a good deal bigger.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.000
And stronger.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.280
It's pushing the first storm through these mountains

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.280
at twice the speed it was moving a few minutes ago.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.280
They're diamagnetic storms, Captain.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.170
Saturated with polaric energy.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:42.540
This is the shuttle?

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.540
Less than 10 kilometers from the first storm.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:51.870
We may not be able to see it yet,

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.870
but it'll be coming through the mountain pass to the north.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.080
We can see it just fine, Captain!

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.000
The storms are throwing up too much interference into the atmosphere.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.740
The shuttle's out of the question.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.790
Captain, these ruins have very thick walls.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.210
You sure will be safe inside.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.130
I'm afraid we're not talking about thunderclouds, Hoshi.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.060
A poleric burst that could short-circuit a shuttle pod

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.400
could do a lot worse to your nervous system.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.860
But, sir, these buildings are over 4,000 years old.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.120
I'm sure they've survived hundreds of these storms.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.050
I've sent Malcolm down to the transporter.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.000
We're going to need to bring you up one-on-one.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.580
that would most likely attract a polaric discharge.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.200
- You have to do this, Hoshi.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.600
- There's no choice.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.400
I'll need you to clear the structure.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.950
- One at a time.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:55.270
- Understood, Captain.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.300
- He's first.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.780
- Have you ever done this?

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.000
- No, but the Captain has, and Malcolm did it twice.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.840
You said there's nothing to it.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.930
Your molecules get pulled apart.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.980
Then they get put back together again.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.720
Do you know how many molecules are made up of?

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.820
Lots.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:11.880
Alright, how many?

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.300
A few trillion.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.270
That's a pretty big jigsaw puzzle.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.650
What if some of the pieces get put in the wrong place?

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.660
You know, I bet a lot of them look real similar.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.500
Starfleet said it's safe.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.540
That's good enough for me.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.370
Okay, okay, but you go first, and if you get to Enterprise one piece, I'll be right behind you.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.120
Fair enough.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.640
to the club. How do those molecules feel? All in the right place?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:30.860
I'll let you know.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:41.590
It's been a long

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:47.490
getting from there to here.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.290
It's been a long time

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:54.900
but my time is finally near.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.970
And I will see my dream

00:04:57.970 --> 00:04:59.670
come alive and last.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.920
Touch the sky

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:07.600
They're not gonna hold me down no more

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.440
They're not gonna change my mind

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.820
Cause I've got

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.000
Come in.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.530
No worse for the wear ensign?

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.330
I guess you could say that, sir.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.180
I'll be at my post in a few minutes, I just want to clean up and change.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.770
I think you've had enough excitement for one afternoon.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.790
The morning will be fine.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.690
Thank you.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:48.560
I assume you and Trip will want to finish your survey tomorrow, weather permitting.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:49.860
Sir?

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.360
You left a shuttle pod down there, remember?

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.970
Somebody's got to go back and get it.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:58.130
I'm sure Commander Tucker can find someone else to hold the second flash unit.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.000
You wouldn't be using the transporter, Hoshi.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:02.190
You'd be taking the other pod.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:04.600
I don't want to get lost.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:05.720
Lost?

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:13.310
Too much excitement for one day.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.910
I could really use some rest, sir.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:17.730
See you in the morning.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.930
- I heard it, come on.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.070
There's no use pretending.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:35.270
Come on, Travis.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.110
- Anyone sitting here?

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:36.950
- Don't you think a Vulcan would see right through that one?

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.130
- But that's what you said, though.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.950
- I don't know, no, no, no, no.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.980
- Is anyone sitting here?

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.250
- No, please.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:47.910
- So what was it like?

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.660
- Travis, I didn't mean to suffer.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.750
- It was very unsettling.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:55.380
Didn't you find it unsettling?

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.840
- For a minute or two, but once I counted my fingers

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.370
and toes.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.000
- I don't know, I just...

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:05.870
don't feel right it was probably that storm you don't forget things like that

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:11.290
too quickly it's not the storms it's the transporter I don't feel like myself

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:15.780
since I went through it now I need to check the medical database and find out

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:19.340
what happened to the people they used they were testing that thing you mean

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:25.550
other than Cyrus Ramsey Cyrus Ramsey I don't tell me you don't know about poor

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:30.000
Cyrus am I supposed to you can't go into survival over

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.220
night without hearing a story about someone seeing Ramsey's molecules

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:39.510
rematerializing on a foggy night. What happened to him? Next thing he'll tell us

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:47.570
you never heard of the Easter Bunny. What happened to him? Madison, Wisconsin. May I

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:55.730
think. 2146. He was a test subject for the first long-range transport. Just 100

00:08:55.730 --> 00:09:00.000
meters. Something went wrong with the pattern bug.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.360
You never re-materialized.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.380
Come on, Oshie.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:08.870
Everybody's heard of Cyrus Ramsey.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:12.480
I must have fallen asleep before the ghost stories.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.640
Where'd you do your survival training?

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.210
Death Valley, California.

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:20.110
Middle of July, naturally.

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:21.650
You?

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:23.500
Captain and I were in the same group.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.010
Alice Springs, Australia.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:28.620
Never saw so many flies in my life.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.510
Biting kind.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.380
- Tucker.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.600
- Storms are breaking up.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:35.660
I don't think we'll have any trouble

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.440
getting you back down in the morning.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.250
- Travis was just telling me he'd like to see the ruins.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.590
- Well, I don't think Hoshi will be joining you.

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.630
- I'll need a pilot to bring the other pod back.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:45.710
- Travis, it is.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.010
You're both in the morning, Archer out.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.830
- Never say I don't take you anywhere.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.300
- You don't take me anywhere.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.950
- See you later.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.810
Doctor?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:06.790
Dr. Phlox?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:18.010
Hello?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.980
I am citizens.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:21.960
Something I can do for you?

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.340
I just looked in there.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:24.260
Were you in there?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.640
Did you hear me come in?

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.150
I was feeding my leeches.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:28.900
Are you alright?

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:30.880
You didn't hear me.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:32.720
I'm right here, Ensign.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.870
Are you not feeling well?

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.080
No, I'm not feeling well.

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:45.960
I dematerialized, and then I rematerialized, and no, I'm not feeling well.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.620
I heard about your ordeal on the surface.

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:50.540
Those storms sounded terrifying.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.350
Doctor, I'm not talking about the storms.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.540
I'm talking about my molecules.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:58.340
Comes it down.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:10:59.920
Let's take a look.

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:15.260
take me a while to account for every molecule but you appear to be in one

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:20.230
piece I don't think you're in danger of becoming the next Cyrus Ramsey don't

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:23.920
tell me they talk about him on Denobula oh I spent nearly nine months on earth

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:30.000
remember I just don't feel right ever since the transport I've been shaking

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.180
Not myself.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.170
Not a single biomolecular anomaly.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:34.910
No?

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.030
How about this?

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.490
A subcutaneous pigmentation.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:40.970
That's not where it used to be.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.250
It was a good centimeter lower.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.240
Well, it looks lovely where it is now.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.340
It's not a joke, doctor.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.560
If that machine could move a birthmark, who knows what else it could do.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.300
I'm telling you I don't feel right.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:00.000
I have a lot of animals to feed before bedtime.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.750
If I were you, I'd get a good night's sleep, hmm?

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:28.110
It's possible my shift starts at 0800.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.380
Now it's in.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.790
I'm sorry, Captain. I don't know what happened.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.680
Tucker and Mayweather have been taken hostage.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.110
Trip got off a short message, but we haven't

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.470
heard anything in the last hour.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.010
Taken hostage by who? The people down there didn't like you

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.050
disturbing their ruins.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.130
People, there wasn't a biosign on the planet.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.040
The chambers you and Mr. Tucker

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.100
photographed contained sacred relics.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.000
Could you possibly know that?

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:00.000
Have you found their biosigns? They're still in the

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.940
complex. I'm trying to isolate the specific

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:05.130
chamber. It's Mayweather's communicator.

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:10.130
Go ahead, Travis.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:17.990
Ensign? I need more.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.590
This is Captain Archer of the Starship

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:26.700
Enterprise. We apologize if

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.000
we've trespassed. My crew

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:41.510
didn't mean any harm I'm sorry sir it's not working I'm gonna need more can I

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:52.020
speak to one of my officers it's not gonna get much better than that

00:13:52.020 --> 00:14:00.000
what's the problem maybe you should forget about the UT just trying

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:21.070
If I went back to the universal translator, maybe I could...

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:23.750
You already tried that. Talk to them.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:24.720
I can't.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.360
Lives are at stake, Ensign.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:30.000
I know. I don't understand what he's saying. I'm...

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.720
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.880
No need to apologize.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.810
Why don't you go back to your quarters, then?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.320
Get some rest.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:41.820
Captain, I realize I overslept.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:43.760
I don't know how it happened.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:47.280
But please, I don't want to go back to my quarters.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.140
Take your calm, my Captain.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.100
Malcolm.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:31.730
Anyone sitting here?

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:36.270
Sub-Commander.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:42.520
Hanson.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.040
Would you like to join me?

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:51.250
Thank you.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:52.250
I would have thought you'd be on the bridge.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:53.740
Why is that?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:56.580
Commander Tucker.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.500
Travis.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:00.000
The hostage situation was resolved.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.620
- They're back on board.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.220
- It's only been an hour since I left the bridge.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.310
What happened?

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.330
- Kermin Baird deciphered their language,

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:09.760
a simple bimodal syntax.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.320
- I don't understand how.

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.250
- With the universal translator.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:14.090
- It's impossible.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.470
I ran every linguistic algorithm.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:18.290
- When the captain agreed to return the soil

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.890
and rock samples and destroy the photographs

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:25.730
that were taken, the hostages were released.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:26.770
- If we've decrypted the language,

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.100
I should get back to the bridge.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:30.000
Sounds like the captain might want to speak with them again.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:32.260
- Captain Archer has asked that you remain off duty

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.830
for the time being.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:42.950
Crewman Baird has been placed in charge of communications.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:47.950
- You should take a look at the secondary couplings.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.130
They're going to need to be aligned.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:49.970
- Awesome.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.640
- Start on C deck and work your way down.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:16.420
What?

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.660
- Can you see me?

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:40.770
- Denson.

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:43.070
- Can you see me?

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:44.110
- Is there something in particular

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:47.150
you'd like me to look at?

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:48.210
- Something's wrong, Doctor.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:51.320
Something's very wrong.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:53.380
Ever since I used that transporter,

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:56.390
nothing has been the way that it's supposed to be.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:58.840
I couldn't translate a simple bimodal syntax,

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.000
but Hooman Baird could.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:05.090
Crimin Bear doesn't know the first thing about our linguistic database.

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:08.990
And Captain Archer told me to stay in my quarters.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:12.290
But my mirror doesn't want to give me a solid reflection.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:18.460
And my shower can't decide whether to bounce off me or go through me.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:21.390
And nobody wants to talk to me.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:25.900
Sometimes I think they don't even see that I'm there.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.580
Turbolift control won't even respond to me.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:30.000
Well, I see you.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:38.970
ensign and the sick bay doors responded when you came in transporter technology is very new

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:44.780
i'm sure humans were equally frightened when the automobile was introduced or the airplane

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:51.160
new forms of transports take a while to get used to i'm not at all surprised at your reaction you

00:19:51.160 --> 00:20:00.000
wouldn't catch me using that apparatus but i can promise you one thing you're in perfect health or neither

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:06.180
transparent nor porous you won't put this on my medical record will you as far as i'm concerned

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:12.060
i didn't even see you come in here not funny doctor i would like to give you a mild sedative

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:17.690
it'll help you get a good night's sleep if it's all the same to you the last thing i need right

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:28.260
now is to be medicated as you wish but stop by in the morning all right first thing thank you doctor

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.480
upside down, Ensign.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.100
I was taught never to contradict a superior officer.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.580
The captain told me what happened.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:51.480
Did they treat you all right?

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:53.470
Didn't even tie us up.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.930
As soon as the captain promised to give them their stuff back,

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.700
they walked us to the shuttle pods,

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:00.000
and away we went.

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:04.820
- I'm sorry, I wasn't more helpful trying to translate.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:05.760
I don't know what happened.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:10.200
- Well, we're safe and sound, that's all that matters.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.470
Have you tried this thing?

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:18.120
- I get motion sickness, remember?

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:21.360
Have you felt okay since we were transported yesterday?

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.830
- Considering that I've been back down to the surface,

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:28.290
kidnapped and released, I've probably had better days.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:35.550
you're not feeling well I didn't think I was but the doctor seems to feel my

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:41.670
symptoms are psychological what kind of symptoms I just haven't been myself

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:50.470
everything's a little off even the laws of physics well in that case you're right you

00:21:50.470 --> 00:22:00.000
shouldn't get on this thing the laws of physics don't apply in here either sorry just trying

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:00.650
to cheer you up.

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:02.760
It's okay.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:05.220
Locke's promises me

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:05.920
I'll be fine.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:07.260
It's gonna be a while

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:07.960
before any of us

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:08.660
gets used to being

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:09.830
taken apart

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:11.550
and put back together again.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:13.900
Seems perfectly natural

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:15.450
to be anxious about it.

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:16.730
I hope it's just

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:17.770
your question of being anxious.

00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:20.660
Well, what else could it be?

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:23.420
I saw my reflection

00:22:23.420 --> 00:22:24.340
become transparent.

00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:26.800
I saw water

00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:28.300
pass right through my hand.

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:30.000
I'm not convinced

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.040
that the transporter put me back the way it's supposed to.

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:36.120
- All the king's horses and all the king's men.

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:39.820
I can see why you might imagine the universe unraveling.

00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:42.740
You're afraid you haven't been put back together, right?

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:45.630
Why assume anything else makes sense?

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:48.540
If I were you, I'd ask the doc for a sedative.

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:51.350
Nothing like crawling into bed.

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:55.280
- You men are all alike. - I'll wait and see.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:57.240
A night's sleep will do you a world of good.

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:20.160
- Thank God you're here.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:22.260
I've been stuck in here for hours, the door control is--

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:25.570
- She was here last night, right over there.

00:24:25.570 --> 00:24:30.000
- Commander, T'Pol to Captain Archer.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:31.660
- Go ahead.

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.020
- Have the security details reported back?

00:24:34.020 --> 00:24:37.900
- No sign of her yet.

00:24:37.900 --> 00:24:40.710
- We've covered the forward section of Sea Deck.

00:24:40.710 --> 00:24:42.290
She's not here.

00:24:42.290 --> 00:24:43.470
- Yes, she is.

00:24:43.470 --> 00:24:45.930
- Have you tried the biosensives again, Captain?

00:24:45.930 --> 00:24:47.870
- Still nothing.

00:24:47.870 --> 00:24:49.930
- I'll go take a look at 'em.

00:24:49.930 --> 00:24:51.610
- I'm going to maintain our present orbit

00:24:51.610 --> 00:24:53.820
until Hoshi turns up.

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:56.280
Paul, meet me in sickbay right away.

00:24:56.280 --> 00:24:56.820
- Yes, sir.

00:25:06.300 --> 00:25:13.040
She came to sickbay after the incident with the storm, then a second time, early last night.

00:25:13.040 --> 00:25:14.950
She wasn't feeling well?

00:25:14.950 --> 00:25:17.250
She said she felt shaky.

00:25:17.250 --> 00:25:19.740
You're aware that was the first time she'd ever transported?

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:20.720
Quite aware.

00:25:20.720 --> 00:25:22.720
I believed that was the source of her anxiety.

00:25:22.720 --> 00:25:27.360
She was convinced her molecules hadn't been reassembled properly.

00:25:27.360 --> 00:25:29.510
I should have taken her more seriously.

00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:33.880
These are the biomolecular scans I took during each of her two visits.

00:25:33.880 --> 00:25:36.340
They seemed perfectly normal at the time.

00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:39.120
I heard she was missing.

00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:42.280
Something made me take a closer look.

00:25:42.280 --> 00:25:45.370
You see these protein filaments?

00:25:45.370 --> 00:25:53.550
Now, look at this.

00:25:53.550 --> 00:25:56.740
I'm gonna need some help here, Phlox.

00:25:56.740 --> 00:25:59.860
Look how much her subcellular membranes have degraded.

00:26:00.640 --> 00:26:02.600
These scans were taken less than 24 hours apart.

00:26:02.740 --> 00:26:04.690
It's virtually impossible.

00:26:05.710 --> 00:26:06.390
What's impossible?

00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:11.800
And since I wasn't imagining it, her molecules are coming apart.

00:26:16.590 --> 00:26:17.970
It's the secondary phase coils.

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:19.800
What about them?

00:26:20.300 --> 00:26:21.650
They're not aligning.

00:26:23.790 --> 00:26:25.110
They're not perfectly synchronized.

00:26:28.140 --> 00:26:30.000
It must have happened right after it came up from the surface.

00:26:30.730 --> 00:26:32.790
If they're not perfectly synchronized.

00:26:33.270 --> 00:26:35.370
The resequencing would start to dissipate.

00:26:35.890 --> 00:26:37.970
Within hours, she'll lose molecular cohesion.

00:26:38.820 --> 00:26:40.550
She didn't want to go first.

00:26:41.740 --> 00:26:43.480
Told her I wouldn't leave her alone.

00:26:44.030 --> 00:26:46.230
That storm coming, but she insisted on going second.

00:26:47.500 --> 00:26:48.760
She wanted to be sure it was working.

00:26:49.520 --> 00:26:50.430
I was safe.

00:26:53.010 --> 00:26:54.010
I'm the one you should be missing.

00:26:54.810 --> 00:26:56.380
Told her to go first.

00:26:58.260 --> 00:26:59.220
She should have listened to me.

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:09.540
wasn't your fault. Take the transporter offline. Figure out what went wrong. Starfleet promised

00:27:09.540 --> 00:27:16.510
me this sort of thing wouldn't happen. Aye, sir. Captain, if there was a loss of molecular

00:27:16.510 --> 00:27:23.140
cohesion, I'm afraid we shouldn't be looking for Hoshi, per se. What should we be looking

00:27:23.140 --> 00:27:30.000
for? Subcellular residue. There wouldn't be anything left by now except for subcellular

00:27:30.960 --> 00:27:35.730
You're wrong, doctor. I'm still in one piece, you just can't see me.

00:27:35.730 --> 00:27:55.860
Have the doctor help you recalibrate the sensors, then start scanning for this messenger.

00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:02.560
Archer to Mayweather.

00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:03.740
Go ahead, sir.

00:28:04.210 --> 00:28:07.860
Prepare to break orbit and resume the previous course.

00:28:08.550 --> 00:28:09.030
Aye, Captain.

00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:15.850
I'll be in my ready room.

00:28:23.540 --> 00:28:26.980
No way to be certain this is her.

00:28:27.320 --> 00:28:28.920
Is it Hoshi's DNA or is it?

00:28:29.250 --> 00:28:30.000
It's difficult to tell.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.790
You can tell. The amino acids are broken down.

00:28:32.790 --> 00:28:35.070
Don't waste your time, it's not me.

00:28:35.070 --> 00:28:38.760
The internal scan said access shaft B7.

00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:43.830
She's gotta be here somewhere.

00:28:43.830 --> 00:28:47.500
You spent a little more time trying to figure out what happened to her.

00:28:47.500 --> 00:28:53.200
Vassage.

00:29:00.410 --> 00:29:05.440
- Lieutenant?

00:29:05.440 --> 00:29:15.350
- Here, doc, over here, what do you think?

00:29:15.350 --> 00:29:19.230
- By isolating the dipeptides,

00:29:19.230 --> 00:29:21.600
now run a comparison with her genetic profile.

00:29:29.330 --> 00:29:30.000
- Why would she have

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:31.400
Come down here.

00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:36.060
What we'll ever know, Commander.

00:29:36.060 --> 00:29:40.610
And Archer will...

00:29:40.610 --> 00:29:44.320
...know she's parents to have this.

00:29:44.320 --> 00:29:47.480
They're both alive, aren't they?

00:29:47.480 --> 00:29:54.570
Yeah, both alive.

00:29:54.570 --> 00:29:56.650
Go ahead, Doc.

00:29:56.650 --> 00:30:00.000
I'm gonna stick around for a minute.

00:30:01.760 --> 00:30:02.530
- I understand.

00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:17.030
- Excuse me?

00:30:17.030 --> 00:30:22.580
- I should have made you go first.

00:30:22.580 --> 00:30:26.690
What could I have been thinking leaving you down there?

00:30:26.690 --> 00:30:28.550
I was the ranking officer.

00:30:30.190 --> 00:30:34.260
I had no business leaving a subordinate in the path of those storms.

00:30:34.260 --> 00:30:36.840
Why didn't you listen to me?

00:30:36.840 --> 00:30:38.360
I told you it'd be safe.

00:31:03.130 --> 00:31:25.250
*Mario plays*

00:31:47.180 --> 00:31:49.120
Captain, I need you to listen to me.

00:31:49.120 --> 00:31:51.320
There are aliens on board from the surface.

00:31:51.320 --> 00:31:55.760
They're planting bombs on D-Deck.

00:31:55.760 --> 00:31:57.970
You've got to hear me, the ship is in danger.

00:32:03.740 --> 00:32:04.980
- Go ahead.

00:32:04.980 --> 00:32:06.990
- Kill her father, sir.

00:32:06.990 --> 00:32:13.150
- Mother isn't home.

00:32:13.150 --> 00:32:15.110
- What time is it there?

00:32:15.110 --> 00:32:20.270
- Nine hundred.

00:32:20.270 --> 00:32:20.550
- I'm through.

00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:35.850
- Good morning, sir.

00:32:35.850 --> 00:32:40.930
- Captain Archer, is everything all right?

00:32:40.930 --> 00:32:47.290
- No, sir, everything is not all right.

00:32:47.290 --> 00:32:50.690
We've had an accident with our transporting device.

00:32:50.690 --> 00:32:54.110
- Transporting device, what is that?

00:32:54.110 --> 00:32:55.510
- You don't have timepiece.

00:32:55.510 --> 00:32:58.090
- A Matterstream converter.

00:32:58.090 --> 00:33:00.000
It was approved for transporting biomass

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:01.220
before we left Earth.

00:33:01.220 --> 00:33:02.700
- Gotta find something that'll get your attention.

00:33:02.700 --> 00:33:04.120
- We've used it a number of times when I--

00:33:04.120 --> 00:33:08.200
- Biomanner, you're referring to produce or people.

00:33:08.200 --> 00:33:10.860
- I'm just trying to explain to you

00:33:10.860 --> 00:33:14.170
that Starfleet told us it was safe.

00:33:14.170 --> 00:33:17.210
- So, what she is saying?

00:33:17.210 --> 00:33:20.820
- No, sir, there was an accident.

00:33:20.820 --> 00:33:29.250
She began to, her molecules began to destabilize.

00:33:30.250 --> 00:33:36.760
molecules what are you talking about captain this isn't easy sir i fought to get hoshi to come on

00:33:36.760 --> 00:33:45.590
this mission i'm responsible for her being out here she's become a member of our family family

00:33:45.590 --> 00:33:52.600
her family not you why are you calling me to say that she has become a member of your family

00:33:52.600 --> 00:33:58.450
i'm sorry captain you are not making any sense we lost hoshi today

00:34:01.530 --> 00:34:03.130
I wish I didn't have to tell you that.

00:34:04.060 --> 00:34:06.150
I was saying Hoshi is dead.

00:34:06.670 --> 00:34:09.240
We're all going to be dead if I can't get him to notice this.

00:34:10.430 --> 00:34:15.360
Maybe he could call us back later this afternoon.

00:34:16.190 --> 00:34:18.050
How about Morse Coat? You know Morse Coat, don't you?

00:34:18.130 --> 00:34:19.930
I must have time to speak with Hoshi's mother.

00:34:20.070 --> 00:34:20.850
Come on, listen.

00:34:21.180 --> 00:34:21.910
This afternoon.

00:34:22.240 --> 00:34:22.790
Can you hear it?

00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:25.190
I'm so sorry.

00:34:26.680 --> 00:34:27.080
So I must.

00:34:41.160 --> 00:34:43.120
It's not supposed to be making that noise, is it?

00:34:43.120 --> 00:34:50.820
S.O.S. S.O.S. It's a call for help.

00:34:50.820 --> 00:34:59.030
I need you to hear it.

00:34:59.030 --> 00:35:00.000
Architut to Paul.

00:35:00.960 --> 00:35:02.930
- Yes, Captain.

00:35:02.930 --> 00:35:04.450
- Did you come in here for a minute?

00:35:04.450 --> 00:35:05.290
- Right away.

00:35:05.290 --> 00:35:06.130
- That's right, show it to her.

00:35:06.130 --> 00:35:10.470
One of you will figure it out.

00:35:10.470 --> 00:35:14.440
- Look at this.

00:35:14.440 --> 00:35:18.490
I've never heard it make that noise before.

00:35:18.490 --> 00:35:20.870
- Plasma circuit's being interrupted.

00:35:20.870 --> 00:35:23.490
I'll ask Commander Tucker to take a look at it.

00:35:23.490 --> 00:35:25.930
- Listen to the pattern.

00:35:25.930 --> 00:35:30.000
Three dots, three dashes, three dots.

00:35:31.720 --> 00:35:35.150
SOS.

00:35:35.150 --> 00:35:36.220
Dots.

00:35:36.220 --> 00:35:38.640
Dots and dashes, Morse code.

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:42.330
It's been used on Earth for centuries.

00:35:42.330 --> 00:35:44.880
It's a distress call.

00:35:44.880 --> 00:35:53.400
What are your memories?

00:35:53.400 --> 00:35:57.720
Sounds like Morse code.

00:36:00.920 --> 00:36:03.340
- This plasma circuit is self-contained.

00:36:03.340 --> 00:36:04.460
No one outside of this room

00:36:04.460 --> 00:36:06.400
could be using it to send a message.

00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:09.550
- I'm not outside this room, I'm right here.

00:36:09.550 --> 00:36:13.480
- It's been a very difficult one.

00:36:13.480 --> 00:36:16.830
Perhaps you should try to get some rest.

00:36:16.830 --> 00:36:24.830
- All right, look at it tomorrow.

00:36:24.830 --> 00:36:26.910
- Tomorrow's too late, they're gonna blow up the ship.

00:36:26.910 --> 00:36:27.880
Captain!

00:36:49.390 --> 00:36:50.900
Lora need chat.

00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:52.660
Gaxad.

00:38:31.280 --> 00:38:31.990
up.

00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:14.760
Robert, his dream is too unstable.

00:39:14.760 --> 00:39:19.530
You can do it instantly.

00:39:19.530 --> 00:39:23.990
He is warm and simple.

00:39:23.990 --> 00:39:26.510
All right, nice work, Malo.

00:39:26.510 --> 00:39:29.130
See, I told you. Piece of cake.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.500
Where are they? We've got to stop them.

00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:32.830
Who?

00:39:32.830 --> 00:39:35.790
You heard me? You can hear me. Do you see me?

00:39:35.790 --> 00:39:37.090
Everything's fine, Hoshi.

00:39:37.090 --> 00:39:39.290
It's not fine, they put a bomb on the warp reactor.

00:39:39.290 --> 00:39:40.090
Who?

00:39:40.090 --> 00:39:41.390
The aliens from the surface.

00:39:41.390 --> 00:39:43.990
There's no one on the surface. It's uninhabited.

00:39:43.990 --> 00:39:47.190
What are you talking about? They kidnapped you and Travis.

00:39:47.190 --> 00:39:48.390
We've got to stop them.

00:39:48.390 --> 00:39:51.290
Hoshi, the transporter was affected by the storms.

00:39:51.290 --> 00:39:54.230
I had some trouble reintegrating your matter stream.

00:39:54.230 --> 00:39:56.070
Trouble?

00:39:56.070 --> 00:39:59.650
You were sort of trapped in the pattern buffer.

00:40:00.440 --> 00:40:07.210
only for a few seconds 8.3 seconds to be precise are you saying that i was just on the surface

00:40:07.210 --> 00:40:24.760
you insisted on going second do you have a mirror what forget it i was sure i was

00:40:24.760 --> 00:40:28.740
going to be the next cyrus ramsey cyrus who

00:40:39.240 --> 00:40:42.950
- So you're saying all of that happened in eight seconds?

00:40:42.950 --> 00:40:44.250
- Actually, it probably happened

00:40:44.250 --> 00:40:46.570
in the last one or two seconds,

00:40:46.570 --> 00:40:49.310
as your matter stream was coalescing.

00:40:49.310 --> 00:40:53.680
She seems fine.

00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:55.140
- Malcolm's recommending some new

00:40:55.140 --> 00:40:59.010
transport protocols to Starfleet.

00:40:59.010 --> 00:41:00.000
He's suggesting

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:05.850
start compressing the transport beam well I hope you don't plan on beaming me

00:41:05.850 --> 00:41:11.420
anywhere for a long time but you said you stepped onto the aliens transporter

00:41:11.420 --> 00:41:16.770
by choice I was trying to save Enterprise sounds like you overcame your

00:41:16.770 --> 00:41:23.080
fear it's all in my head remember doesn't matter you were afraid of getting lost

00:41:23.080 --> 00:41:29.090
afraid of disappearing but you still climbed onto that platform real or not

00:41:30.220 --> 00:41:32.680
- If it's all the same to you, sir,

00:41:32.680 --> 00:41:36.840
I'd like to stick to shuttle pods for the time being.

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:41.060
- Come on, let's go to the bridge.

00:41:41.060 --> 00:41:43.700
- Captain, if you don't mind.
